# Tenancy

Every method here takes `ownerId` as its first argument and puts it in the
WHERE clause. There is deliberately no `findById(id)`: that shape invites
"load now, check ownership later", which is how cross-tenant reads ship.

The two genuinely tenant-free lookups carry an `Unscoped` suffix, and the
`no-unscoped-repository-access` rule confines them to the public read path.

A row that belongs to another tenant is reported as not found, never as
forbidden. Telling a stranger an id exists is itself a leak.
